module async/atomic v1.0.0;
import "io/stream" take Closing;

/*
=head1 NAME

async/atomic - shared single-value effect capability

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Atomic(value: initial) creates an initialized cell. value() observes its current
value; replace(value) publishes one complete value. compare_and_replace(expected,
revised) publishes only when the current value equals expected, returning true on
success and false on mismatch. Equality is Okkama's existing strict structural
comparison; incomparable values raise a programming failure without publication.
Equal replacement is a successful publication. This is value CAS, not an ABA-safe
revision protocol: applications requiring monotonicity store and validate their
own revision as part of T. Atomic capabilities themselves compare by identity.

All operations are synchronous, have no suspension point, and are linearizable
among tasks sharing one interpreter. Subsequent observations see the complete
publication. No cross-process/shared-memory or host-thread guarantee is provided.
A sequence of operations is not a transaction. No callbacks run inside an operation.

Returned values are ordinary Okkama values, not mutable references into the cell.
Nested effect capabilities remain shared. Stored resource capabilities are borrowed:
their owner's close/defer/destroy contract still applies; Atomic does not acquire
resource ownership or extend scoped resource lifetimes. Prefer immutable snapshots.

close() is explicit and idempotent, drops the stored value, and affects all aliases.
All subsequent reads and writes throw AtomicClosed. Dropping an alias does not
close the cell; no OS resource or waiter requires implicit destroy. No null/empty
sentinel can be read. The cell's identity is stable; object fields remain immutable.

=cut
*/
object Atomic<T> does Closing {
    Atomic(value is T) {}
    value() is T { panic "Atomic.value is a VM intrinsic"; }
    replace(value is T) is void { panic "Atomic.replace is a VM intrinsic"; }
    compare_and_replace(expected is T, revised is T) is bool {
        panic "Atomic.compare_and_replace is a VM intrinsic";
    }
    closed() is bool { panic "Atomic.closed is a VM intrinsic"; }
    close() is void { panic "Atomic.close is a VM intrinsic"; }
}
object AtomicClosed does Error {
    AtomicClosed();
    text() is string { "atomic state is closed"; }
}
